
title: Holding APRA Together
is-card: true
tags: apra_party_affairs
view-if: party_card_available = 1

= One Party, Many Ambitions

APRA has returned to government, but winning an election does not guarantee internal unity.

Party organisers, labour supporters, parliamentary representatives and the president's advisers may disagree about appointments, economic policy and the direction of the administration.

The president must manage these competing interests while maintaining a workable governing party.

- @apra_unity_meeting: Convene the party leadership.
- @apra_unity_compromise: Negotiate a shared programme.

@apra_unity_meeting
title: Convene the Party Leadership
on-arrival: {!
Q.party_unity = Math.min(100, Q.party_unity + 3);
Q.party_card_available = 0;
!}

You bring the leadership together to discuss the government's priorities. The meeting provides an opportunity to build cooperation within APRA.

- @main: Return to the presidential desk

@apra_unity_compromise
title: Negotiate a Shared Programme
on-arrival: {!
Q.party_unity = Math.min(100, Q.party_unity + 1);
Q.support = Math.min(100, Q.support + 2);
Q.party_card_available = 0;
!}

You seek agreement between competing party interests. The compromise helps preserve unity, although the underlying disagreements have not disappeared.

- @main: Return to the presidential desk
